Toolchain, absorbed by the files beside his tree rather than by edits:
  - his entrypoint runs as he runs it: `node --experimental-strip-types
    src/runtime/main.ts <mode>`. Node 22.12 or newer here (his package.json
    says 22.18, where the flag is on by default; the explicit flag covers
    22.12 and is what his Dockerfile passes anyway).
  - scripts/run.mjs maps SERVICING_DATABASE_URL, SERVICING_PORT and
    SERVICING_API_TOKEN onto the DATABASE_URL, PORT and API_TOKEN his config
    reads, so his names never collide with our API's.
  - scripts/test.mjs runs his tests as his (node --test, one database per
    file cloned from a migrated template) on a database beside ours, and
    leaves out the seven suites that build his Next.js apps under Chromium.
  - tsconfig.check.json extends his tsconfig and excludes the one file that
    imports his borrower app; playwright-core is a devDependency because
    three of his suites and one tool import its types.
  - eslint and Prettier skip every copied directory (root eslint.config.mjs
    and .prettierignore say why), and the repo-walking tests in apps/api
    skip them by name.

License: the source repository carries no LICENSE file. Doug's request that
this be integrated is what the vendoring rests on; ask him to add one when
